                           "Duration": 32.2,
                           "TextFadeDuration": 32.0,
                           "FadeInTime": 0.2,
                           "FadeOutTime": 0.2,
                           "String": "Central Italy, 509 to 290 BCE\n\nLucius Tarquinius, the last King of Rome, has been deposed! The new Roman Republic, under the leadership of the Senate, has many enemies. The nearby Etruscan kings envy Rome's key position on the hills overlooking the Tiber River. They seek to dominate Rome as they did during the age of our forefathers. The various tribes of Italy—Samnites, Umbrians, Campanians, and others—also threaten the growing city-state. Rome will not be built in a day, but the defenses of the city must be.",
                           "ImageRect": {
